## Why This Is Asked
Tests the ability to design a practical, testable fair-use layer for a multi-tenant LLM gateway with billing considerations.

## Key Concepts
- Per-tenant quotas and burst handling using a token bucket
- Isolation of prompts and responses per tenant
- Simple REST API for quota status and consumption
- Observability and a minimal test plan for bucket behavior

## Code Example
```javascript
class TokenBucket {
  constructor(capacity, refillPerMs) {
    this.capacity = capacity;
    this.tokens = capacity;
    this.refillPerMs = refillPerMs;
    this.lastRefill = Date.now();
  }
  tick() {
    const now = Date.now();
    const elapsed = now - this.lastRefill;
    const refill = Math.floor(elapsed * this.refillPerMs);
    if (refill > 0) {
      this.tokens = Math.min(this.capacity, this.tokens + refill);
      this.lastRefill = now;
    }
  }
  tryConsume(n = 1) {
    this.tick();
    if (this.tokens >= n) {
      this.tokens -= n;
      return true;
    }
    return false;
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question probes practical reliability design for LLM gateways, focusing on per-tenant isolation, simple fault handling, and testability—core beginner-to-intermediate LLm-ops concerns.

## Key Concepts
- Per-tenant circuit breakers and state management
- Retry with exponential backoff and jitter
- Graceful failover to cached/cheaper models
- Lightweight data models and testability

## Code Example
```javascript
// Lightweight per-tenant circuit breaker skeleton
class CircuitBreaker {
  constructor(threshold=5, windowMs=60000) {
    this.threshold = threshold; this.windowMs = windowMs;
    this.failures = {}; // tenantId -> [timestamps]
  }
  recordFailure(tid){
    const now = Date.now();
    this.failures[tid] = (this.failures[tid]||[]).concat(now);
  }
  isOpen(tid){
    const now = Date.now();
    const arr = (this.failures[tid]||[]).filter(t=>now-t<=this.windowMs);
    return arr.length >= this.threshold;
  }
}
```

